From c64501ba8e85bafb21deb3ec782d31fc76ce1d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:12:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LAN resolver health check: a primary/standby for the router's
 DNS list, and a strict-order switch

dnsmasq keeps no memory of an upstream that stopped answering: in strict
order every fresh query starts at the first server again, only a client
retransmission moves it along, and its own fast retries (on with DNSSEC)
re-send to the same server. A LAN resolver such as AdGuard going silent
therefore costs a client timeout per uncached name, and a client that lists
the router second needs three attempts before dnsmasq's second server
answers - past dnsmasq's 10-s query lifetime on Linux/Android.

rc/rdnshc.c (applet rdnshc, started from start_services in router mode,
restart_rdnshc from the page): probes one named IPv4 server with a real A
query every reaper_dnshc_interval s (timeout reaper_dnshc_timeout ms; any
reply counts unless reaper_dnshc_strict). After reaper_dnshc_fail misses it
moves that server's lines to the end of /tmp/resolv.dnsmasq and
/tmp/resolv.conf under the resolv lock and reloads dnsmasq; after
reaper_dnshc_recover hits it rebuilds both through update_resolvconf() and
reloads. Re-asserts every tick while demoted (wan_up and the VPN clients
rewrite the file), adopts a demotion across a restart (/tmp/rdnshc.state),
restores when switched off or retargeted, logs every transition, publishes
"up|down <s> <alive>" in reaper_dnshc_state. Not wanduck's dns_probe, which
resolves through the router and only feeds WAN state.

services.c: strict-order emitted in the main dnsmasq config behind
reaper_dns_strict. defaults.c: the nine keys. Advanced_System_Content.asp:
a "Reaper resolver health check" block right under the stock Network
Monitoring row, with its own explanation of the difference, the eight
fields, a live Status line, and an "Upstream order" row for strict-order;
its own init (inline + load listener) so a stock init failure cannot hide
it; restart_rdnshc / restart_dnsmasq appended to the apply only when our
fields changed. RDHC_1-19 in all 25 packs, translated.

Gates: static checks 11/11, langcheck 0, csrfcheck 0, page JS parses,
cppcheck quiet, dicts lockstep 6886; mock-previewed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
